  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine $(\\mathrm{E})$ is working between two temperatures 473 K and 273 K . In a new system two engines - engine $E_1$ works between 473 K to 373 K and engine $E_2$ works between 373 K to 273 K .\nIf $\\eta_{12}, \\eta_1$ and $\\eta_2$ are the efficiencies of the engines $E, E_1$ and $E_2$, respectively, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BcDdK",
      "text": "$\\eta_{12}=\\eta_1 \\eta_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FfVwB",
      "text": "$\\eta_{12} \\geq \\eta_1+\\eta_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "99TEI",
      "text": "$\\eta_{12}=\\eta_1+\\eta_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z9LCx",
      "text": "$\\eta_{12} \\lt \\eta_1+\\eta_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Efficiencies of a carnot engine $\\eta=1-\\frac{T_{\\text {sink }}}{T_{\\text {source }}}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\Rightarrow & \\eta_1=1-\\frac{373 \\mathrm{~K}}{473 \\mathrm{~K}}=\\frac{100}{473} \\\\\n& \\eta_2=1-\\frac{273 \\mathrm{~K}}{373 \\mathrm{~K}}=\\frac{100}{373} \\\\\n& \\eta_{12}=1-\\frac{273 \\mathrm{~K}}{473 \\mathrm{~K}}=\\frac{100}{473} \\\\\n& \\eta_{12}-\\eta_1=\\frac{200}{473}-\\frac{100}{473}=\\frac{100}{473} < \\frac{100}{373} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\eta_{12}-\\eta_1 < \\eta_2 \\\\\n\\text { or } & \\eta_{12} < \\eta_1+\\eta_2\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
